### Two things you should know before you read

**This item had a real incident, and it is on the record deliberately.** On the drill's first run,
before the sensor honoured the override, a synthetic 95 percent reading was written into the live
snapshot the founder's status line maintains — which can park real work. It self-healed and two
permanent guards were added: a static check that the sensor takes its path from the library rather
than spelling one out, and a live canary that aborts the run. Claim 15 and claim 28 are the ones
that carry this. Grade them hard: the guard on the failure that actually happened is the one worth
your attention.

**The runtime proof is deliberately INCOMPLETE, and the record is supposed to say so.** Plan step 10
drives a headless run to prove the deployed hook entries load and fire. Three entry shapes were
proven; the two alarm entries delivered nothing and **the cause was never established**. The
orchestrator ruled the entry ships as built with the claim narrowed, because the live check is
impossible before merge — the committed settings carry main-checkout paths that are live only after
merge. Read `plan.md`, `goal-evidence.md` and `gate2-rulings.md` (ADDENDUM 3) for what the item
says about this, and grade the CODE against it. **The place to look hardest is any sentence that
quietly upgrades "works in isolation" into "works".**

Do not run the probe, and do not run the test suite. Execution evidence belongs to the required CI
check, not to you.

