  16: # The lesson is general: grepping for an API misses code that reimplemented it.
  17: #
  18: # COST MATTERS HERE. Claude Code spawns a fresh PowerShell for every refresh, which on Windows is
  19: # already a few hundred milliseconds; each extra subprocess is paid on every keystroke-ish redraw
  20: # and shows up as a client that looks perpetually busy. So: ONE git call (rev-parse takes several
  21: # arguments at once), and no `git status --porcelain` - the dirty marker was the least valuable
  22: # of the fields and by far the most expensive.
  23: #
  24: # Never throws. A status line that errors is noise in the founder's face on every keystroke.
