   1: # stamp-hook.ps1 - UserPromptSubmit hook: the WORKING ON stamp.
   2: #
   3: # Prints EXACTLY TWO LINES before every prompt, always, in one fixed format:
   4: #
   5: #   WORKING ON  <root> > <parents...> > <item>
   6: #   IN          wt <folder> - branch <branch>
   7: #
   8: # Line 1 is the conclusion. Line 2 is WHAT THE CONCLUSION WAS DERIVED FROM. That pairing is the
   9: # whole point: every past incident was line 1 disagreeing with line 2 while only line 1 was
  10: # visible. Anything else - a conflict, an unresolved chain, a git state - APPENDS below. The two
  11: # lines never change shape, so they are always in the same place and always mean the same thing.
  12: #
  13: # ATTRIBUTION IS DERIVED, NEVER DECLARED. cwd -> git worktree -> branch -> exactly one item id.
  14: # The held item (written by /work) is a CROSS-CHECK ONLY: it can raise CONFLICT or fill a gap the
  15: # branch left empty, but it can NEVER override the branch. A stale held item therefore makes the
  16: # stamp louder, never wronger - the inverse of the folder-keyed binding this replaces, which
  17: # silently substituted itself for reality (AI4DEV-24: a whole run stamped against the wrong item).
  18: #
  19: # NEVER CALLS LINEAR. Titles and chains come from a cache written by /work. A cache miss degrades
  20: # to the bare item id with a note - it never guesses, and it never blocks.
  21: #
  22: # NEVER SILENT. On any failure this prints "stamp error: <what>" rather than something plausible.
  23: # The dangerous failure is not a wrong stamp; it is no stamp becoming normal, after which nobody
  24: # reads the line at all.
