  62: $raw = [IO.File]::ReadAllText($committed)
  63: # JSON escapes each backslash, so the prefix appears doubled inside the file.
  64: #
  65: # PLAIN STRING Replace, NEVER -replace. This line used `-replace`, which is the REGEX operator:
  66: # the pattern '\\' matches one backslash, but a .NET replacement string takes a backslash
  67: # literally, so '\\\\' inserts FOUR. The probe searched for C:\\\\Users\\\\... while the file
  68: # holds C:\\Users\\... , nothing matched, and the "twin" came out a byte-for-byte copy still
  69: # carrying MAIN-checkout paths - two of which do not exist in main, so those entries pointed at
